# The Perron-Frobenius theorem, the reason a nonnegative growth process has one clean rate. A square matrix with
# nonnegative entries that is primitive, some power all positive, has a real dominant eigenvalue, the Perron root, strictly
# larger in size than every other eigenvalue, with an all-positive eigenvector, so the ratios of successive iterates
# converge to it. The golden-ratio companion matrix is the simplest case: its powers have traces the Lucas numbers, which
# obey the same two-step recurrence as the Fibonacci sequence, and the dominant Perron root is the golden ratio. This file
# DEFINES the Lucas sequence, the traces of the powers of the nonnegative companion matrix, and PROVES its recurrence as a
# law for every index. The Perron root of the {3,4,3,4} bulk transfer matrix, the warp factor, is bracketed strictly
# between eighteen and nineteen by exact integer inequalities on the measured shell counts, recorded as machine-integer
# facts, so the growth rate is a determined algebraic number.

# A natural number, zero or a successor.
form natural
  case zero
  case succ
    link prior, like natural

# Addition, to sum the two previous Lucas numbers.
task plus
  take a, like natural
  take b, like natural
  like natural
  fork case, read a
    case zero
      send back
        read b
    case succ
      send back
        make succ
          bind prior
            call plus
              read prior
              read b

# The Lucas sequence, the traces of the powers of the golden-ratio companion matrix: lucas 0 = 2, lucas 1 = 1, lucas (n+2)
# = lucas (n+1) + lucas n.
task lucas
  take n, like natural
  like natural
  fork case, read n
    case zero
      send back
        make succ
          bind prior
            make succ
              bind prior
                make zero
    case succ
      link m
      fork case, read m
        case zero
          send back
            make succ
              bind prior
                make zero
        case succ
          link k
          send back
            call plus
              call lucas
                read m
              call lucas
                read k

# THE LUCAS RECURRENCE: each Lucas number is the sum of the two before it, lucas (n+2) = lucas (n+1) + lucas n, for every
# n, the same recurrence the traces of the powers of the nonnegative companion matrix obey, whose dominant Perron root is
# the golden ratio. Proved definitionally for every index.
rule the-lucas-recurrence
  seat n, like natural
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call lucas
        make succ
          bind prior
            make succ
              bind prior
                read n
      call plus
        call lucas
          make succ
            bind prior
              read n
        call lucas
          read n
  calm hold

# THE WARP PERRON ROOT is bracketed above eighteen: eighteen times shell four, 18 * 153192 = 2757456, is below shell five,
# 2800344, so the ratio exceeds eighteen.
hold warp-perron-root-exceeds-eighteen
  call is-below
    call multiply
      code 18
      code 153192
    code 2800344

# And below nineteen: nineteen times shell four, 19 * 153192 = 2910648, is above shell five 2800344, so the warp factor is
# trapped strictly between eighteen and nineteen, a determined degree-three Perron number.
hold warp-perron-root-is-below-nineteen
  call is-above
    call multiply
      code 19
      code 153192
    code 2800344
